+# 02: Downgrades, lateral changes and interval switches take effect at renewal
+
+**What to build:** A customer can downgrade, make a lateral change (another plan with the same monthly list price), or switch between monthly and annual billing. Nothing is billed when they ask. The request becomes the subscription's scheduled change, the customer keeps their current plan until the period they paid for ends, and the next renewal moves them to the new plan and interval and bills its full price. Unused time is never refunded (ADR 0001). See the spec (Downgrade, lateral change, interval switch; Subscription model; Renewal).
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Upgrade with a prorated invoice)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] `Subscription` has optional `scheduled_plan_code` and `scheduled_interval` fields, defaulting to `None`. Constructing it with one set and the other not raises `ValueError`.
+- [ ] A downgrade (lower monthly list price) returns `None` and records no invoice. The current plan, interval and period don't change, and the scheduled change holds the target plan and interval.
+- [ ] A lateral change (different plan, same monthly list price, e.g. pro → "team" at 30 a month or 270 a year) behaves the same as a downgrade.
+- [ ] A pure interval switch (same plan) behaves the same way, in both directions (monthly → annual and annual → monthly).
+- [ ] A downgrade combined with switching to annual is stored as one scheduled change with the new plan and the annual interval.
+- [ ] The scheduled change is classified by monthly list price whatever the current or target interval. For example, pro annual → basic monthly is a downgrade.
+- [ ] When `renew_due` renews a subscription with a scheduled change:
+  - [ ] the subscription moves to the scheduled plan and interval and the scheduled change is cleared;
+  - [ ] the new period starts on the old period end and its length follows the new interval;
+  - [ ] the renewal invoice is for the new plan's full price at the new interval, dated on the period start.
+- [ ] A scheduled plan retired between the request and the renewal is still applied.
+- [ ] When renewals are caught up, the scheduled change applies to the first missed renewal only, and later catch-up renewals use the changed plan and interval.
+- [ ] A canceled subscription with a scheduled change is never renewed, so the change is never applied.
+- [ ] Downgrades, lateral changes and interval switches are no longer rejected with `InvalidPlanChange`.
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `plan-changes` (commits c742d1a, 3731726; review follow-ups in cc06959).
