+# 04: Plan changes during a trial
+
+**What to build:** A customer in a free trial can change plan, interval or both, and the change takes effect immediately. Nothing has been paid yet, so nothing is billed, nothing is prorated, and the trial end date stays the same. When the trial ends, the customer is billed the full price of whichever plan and interval they're on by then. See the spec (Trial).
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Upgrade with a prorated invoice)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] During a trial, an upgrade applies the new plan immediately, records no invoice, and returns `None`.
+- [ ] During a trial, a downgrade and a lateral change also apply immediately (they aren't scheduled), with no invoice and `None` returned.
+- [ ] During a trial, an interval switch applies immediately, with no invoice and `None` returned.
+- [ ] After any change during a trial, the subscription is still trialing and its trial start and end dates are unchanged.
+- [ ] After any change during a trial, no scheduled change is left on the subscription.
+- [ ] At trial end, `renew_due` bills the full price of the plan and interval chosen during the trial, and the first paid period's length follows that interval.
+- [ ] Ticket 01's validation still applies during a trial:
+  - [ ] same plan and same interval → `InvalidPlanChange`
+  - [ ] retired target → `PlanNotAvailable`
+  - [ ] a trial whose end is on or before today and hasn't been renewed → `InvalidPlanChange`
+  - [ ] each rejection leaves the subscription untouched
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `plan-changes` (commits 58b7894; review follow-ups in cc06959).
